Kf8 {... here we go again ...} 9. h4 c5 10. Bd3 Nxd2 11. Kxd2 Nc6 12. Rh3 c4
13. Bf1 {... an experiment - but not a successful one ...} Ne7 14. h5 b5 15.
Nf3 a5 16. a3 Rb8 17. Rb1 Rg8 18. Nh4 Nf5 19. Nxf5 exf5 20. Qf4 Be6 21. Be2 {
... It's fairly level now - Black followed a plan invented by Tarrasch and
employed by Korchnoi.  I used to prefer the Winawer myself (believing 3....
Nf6 4.e5 to be too dangerous). In these days of modern computer software,
Stockfish gives the final position as "slight White advantage" -  (AFB).}
